<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>'Israeli president trying to form unity govt: They will not need Arab parties nor Orthodox parties'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ff3bf99bcabca9e4a251ead2acd39a4e08977ff15f252da2f055b4a052aa6a5</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T15:11:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israeli-president-trying-to-form-unity-govt-they-will-not-need-arab-parties-nor-orthodox-parties" /><summary type="html">Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Tamar Sebok, correspondent for the Israeli daily Yedioth Ahronoth based in France. In an Israeli election marked by political uncertainty, unusually high voter participation and a significant mobilisation of Arab voters, the struggle for power extends far beyond the ballot box. As  Sebok explains, the decisive question is not necessarily which party wins the most seats, but which political leader can assemble a viable governing coalition.

“You don't know until the coalition is formed who really won,” Sebok observes, capturing the fundamental uncertainty of Israel's parliamentary system. “It's not a question of having the most mandates. It's the question of what kind of acceptance you get from the other parties.”

Her analysis illuminates a central paradox of coalition politics: smaller parties can exercise influence disproportionate to their electoral strength when larger parties depend on them to secure a parliamentary majority. As Sebok puts it, “The small parties who are the balance have a lot more power than the big ones. It's a contradiction.”

Particularly significant is Sebok's insistence that public declarations excluding cooperation with Arab parties should not necessarily be understood as definitive. Recalling the coalition negotiations of 2021, she argues that the boundaries of political cooperation can shift considerably once electoral campaigning gives way to the practical demands of government formation.

“The Arab parties have never been that strong,” she notes, before offering a conclusion that encapsulates both the uncertainty and the possibilities of the political moment: “So everything is open.”</summary></entry><entry><title>Top tips for a safe Halloween online</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ae99c7b18521c9eec2b6d05db0fcf577cc99e1acb8ac6d1136842791a66df12</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T15:01:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261028-top-tips-for-a-safe-halloween-online" /><summary type="html">With Halloween just around the corner, digital parenting coach Dr Elizabeth Milovidov gives us some expert tips on managing your child's digital safety while still letting them have fun during the spooky October holiday.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Spanish Transport Minister gives press conference on train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:309ed427d1c4331c38659d9994f5885aa5c247b769838bc6960c53e67929ab24</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:43:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-replay-spanish-transport-minister-gives-press-conference-on-train-crash" /><summary type="html">A high-speed train collision south of Madrid killed 64 people and injured scores more on Wednesday (October 28), with the toll likely to rise, authorities said in one of Europe's deadliest such disasters this century. Spanish Transport Minister Oscar Puente gave some details in a press conference.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain: Dozens killed after one high-speed train slams into another</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c2c49c01c15657dea79b7b18e6cfd7b05b654e93400fd22dfa4f66cb68f62c3</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:34:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-dozens-killed-after-one-high-speed-train-slams-into-another" /><summary type="html">Spain suffered its second deadly high-speed train accident this year when one train on Wednesday, October 28, slammed into another that had stopped on the tracks, with the impact shredding cars and killing at least 64 people. The accident comes with memories still fresh of another crash between high-speed trains in southern Spain in January. France 24's correspondent in Madrid Sarah Morris gives us the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain: At least 64 dead in high-speed train crash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d02e3f5443784ddda3dadcb6ae9ebef9a436a4a731352bfae4a383679fdd59ea</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:33:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-spain-at-least-64-dead-in-high-speed-train-crash" /><summary type="html">In Spain, a high-speed train slammed into the rear of another train that had stopped, derailing two cars and killing at least 64 people on Wednesday, October 28. The central government’s office for Castilla La Mancha confirmed the death toll had risen. It is the second major train accident in Spain this year.</summary></entry><entry><title>West Bank: settlers using drones to monitor Palestinians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c420459e163632e9c4df26df0c3b5653fe518ce3aa51c2eac82a667156f4542</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T13:39:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261028-west-bank-settlers-using-drones-to-monitor-palestinians" /><summary type="html">"We feel like we’re being watched all the time." In the occupied West Bank, Palestinian farmers are speaking out against the extensive use of drones by Israeli settlers and the Israeli military. According to activists and researchers, this practice is aimed, in part, at monitoring new Palestinian construction. In 2026, the Israeli government allocated a budget of 50 million shekels (over 14 million euros) to outposts and illegal settlements in the West Bank to fund so-called "security" equipment—which includes these drones.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Death toll from train collision in central Spain rises to 64, regional government says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74fe5145c583b47c0d86bbd6e914381cf77f572b0ba4e7aff6bf0e1c00b96d1c</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T13:11:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261028-two-high-speed-trains-collide-in-southern-spain-rail-operator-says" /></entry><entry><title>'No clear winner' from Israeli election, expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f6babe4508918f987db7e75accc7cadfddd4ea71fee7cc58409057023929922</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T12:49:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261028-no-clear-winner-from-israeli-election-expert-says" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, we focus on the results of the election in Israel. For analysis, we speak to Yossi Mekelberg, senior consulting fellow at Chatham House's Middle East and North Africa Programme. He tells us there is "no clear winner" from the country's pivotal vote.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Melania Trump-brokered local ceasefire holds for second day</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02c433ce9239c75fcd92f44589a171fd1d01431b8b7c6ceb4138a76e21d4d40d</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T12:42:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-ukraine-melania-trump-brokered-local-ceasefire-holds-for-second-day" /><summary type="html">There ​have been ​no breaches of the US-brokered local ceasefire ​around ‌the ⁠Russian-occupied town of Oleshky ‌in southern Ukraine during its first 30 hours, ​Ukraine's human rights ‌ombudsman Dmytro Lubinets said on ‌Wednesday. A ceasefire has ​been agreed until November 1 to ​allow residents of ​the frontline ​town – who had ​been unable to leave amid near-uninhabitable conditions – to evacuate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Mbappé's China faux pas: When the sports world collides with the complexities of geopolitics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0ef499866f9230788211efa543940aee5260df41259e6864e8a1f51209f7d9a</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T12:20:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261028-mbapp%C3%A9-s-china-faux-pas-when-the-sports-world-collides-with-the-complexities-of-geopolitics" /><summary type="html">François Picard welcomes Igor Mladenovic, a French-Serbian sports writer, sports business analyst and former football commentator based in Luxembourg. For Mladenovic, the backlash in China over Kylian Mbappé's playful reference to a meme depicting him in the likeness of Mao Zedong illustrates a dilemma of the digital age: How a seemingly innocuous anecdote from a football superstar can escalate into a geopolitical firestorm.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Mbappé's China faux pas: When the sports world collides with the complexities of geopolitics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:606a824f1e5c31fbee4f7ecf408b073a9b64397e9354fc8da65b9e80ee397fc3</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T12:17:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-mbapp%C3%A9-s-china-faux-pas-when-the-sports-world-collides-with-the-complexities-of-geopolitics" /><summary type="html">François Picard welcomes Igor Mladenovic, a French-Serbian sports writer, sports business analyst and former football commentator based in Luxembourg. For Mladenovic, the backlash in China over Kylian Mbappé's playful reference to a meme depicting him in the likeness of Mao Zedong illustrates a dilemma of the digital age: How a seemingly innocuous anecdote from a football superstar can escalate into a geopolitical firestorm.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli election: PM loses a significant number of seats since 2022 election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4813e57dc2979d9e564730928278da41c71d9fc67124b1508f21835c72a017c</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T11:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israeli-election-pm-loses-a-significant-number-of-seats-since-2022-election" /><summary type="html">Israel was counting votes on Wednesday after pivotal elections in which exit polls showed no clear winner. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s bloc appears to have lost a significant number of seats compared with the previous election in 2022. France 24’s International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Flavio Bolsonaro leaves Argentina for alleged US asylum after defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bd38b814999ad09cfce5faf5baa2be5c997c5b30fa008033347939ef98f30c5</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T11:43:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-leaves-argentina-for-alleged-us-asylum-after-defeat" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro, who lost Brazil's runoff election to incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva on Sunday, boarded a flight to Ecuador after arriving in Argentina on Tuesday night, October 27. He is expected to land in Miami, as the US State Department said it would issue visas to him and his family. France 24's correspondent in Rio de Janeiro Tim Vickery reports the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli election: As votes are counted, no clear winner emerges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bec08fac9e2f907fb0d9eeddc0b4370ee5d5e6a72857b013f8becc62ddb3fc88</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T11:32:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-israeli-election-as-votes-are-counted-no-clear-winner-emerges" /><summary type="html">Anxious Israelis watched election results take shape Wednesday after the highest turnout in over a quarter-century, as no clear winner emerged and weeks of negotiating could lie ahead for Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and an array of opposition parties trying to unseat him. France 24 correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky reports the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Bolsonaro defeated and on the run</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e013786e40c908fbb6356ee5877627e90b639c7c708627d620c6ec3a4ba2e651</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T11:30:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-bolsonaro-defeated-and-on-the-run" /><summary type="html">Defeated far-right presidential candidate Flávio Bolsonaro has left Brazil for the United States, despite a court order barring him from leaving the country. The son of jailed former president Jair Bolsonaro has yet to concede defeat in Sunday’s election and is under investigation in Brazil for alleged corruption and money laundering. Antonia Kerrigan has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>India: Over 180,000 evacuated on east coast as massive cyclone hits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3267bacb2d7e8a54a3ceee24cce08addf74c2497204efb6f40a04105be816bca</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T11:28:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-india-over-180-000-evacuated-on-east-coast-as-massive-cyclone-hits" /><summary type="html">A 125-kilometer-per-hour cyclone hit the southeastern coast of India on Wednesday, October 28, as authorities warned of localised flooding and the uprooting of power and communications poles. At least 180,000 people have been evacuated, while neighbouring Sri Lanka and Nepal have also issued weather warnings. Camille Corcoran reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Ceasefire holds for its first 30 hours in occupied Oleshky</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:285b32535ce602a9cd5c5958a9b11a624bc1e95a9b57c9c3baebbc0a64aad1e1</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:46:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-ukraine-ceasefire-holds-for-its-first-30-hours-in-occupied-oleshky" /><summary type="html">A local ceasefire in the Russian-occupied southern Ukrainian city of Oleshky held through its first day and night, despite continued fighting between Moscow and Kyiv elsewhere. The truce, which began on Tuesday in the devastated city, is expected to remain in place until Sunday. Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Slashing of food stamps in Arizona angers voters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99ed15778bed2e39d20b7b60a2a14efc1e7ec31bccc15b2659fb57fce2a4a3da</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:43:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261028-us-midterms-slashing-of-food-stamps-in-arizona-angers-voters" /><summary type="html">With the US midterm elections just under a week away, the cost of living has emerged as a key campaign issue. In Arizona, many Americans are criticising the administration’s decision to slash food stamps, which has had significant consequences for the poorest. Camille Corcoran reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel: Netanyahu edges closer to a majority</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c15e81a294893e54b3a6b002505c20a0effde11c6d732ae42ee61b4e7b8d81f8</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-netanyahu-edges-closer-to-a-majority" /><summary type="html">The final results are expected tonight or tomorrow morning. For now, the picture is looking increasingly favourable for Benjamin Netanyahu and his bloc, but the Israeli prime minister is still short of a clear victory, as he needs 61 seats to secure a parliamentary majority. He addressed his supporters at the National Congress Centre at around 3 a.m. local time. France 24’s Clovis Casali joins us live from Jerusalem with the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain: Local authorities confirm at least 10 dead in train accident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e02bc5ff8f27b8bbc59fc211e6b872a8cdce84e0ee34f2eb3ef3920fbb3072cc</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:17:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-local-authorities-confirm-at-least-10-dead-in-train-accident" /><summary type="html">Two trains travelling in opposite directions have collided in southern Spain, on the route between Madrid and Seville. At least 10 deaths have been confirmed, although some media reports put the toll as high as 39. The crash brings back painful memories of a deadly train accident in Córdoba in January. The cause of the collision remains unknown. France 24 correspondent Sarah Morris joins us live from Madrid with the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli election: 'Wishful thinking' for pro- and anti-Netanyahu parties?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67798016af182721afd30df4e8eb49c0fd3dc9e4bc87f87ba42756be744475de</id><updated>2026-10-28T15:13:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:15:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261028-israeli-election-wishful-thinking-for-pro-and-anti-netanyahu-parties" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, October 28: Papers react to the ongoing election results in Israel. Next: Macklemore's Free Palestine tour is coming to Paris. Also: antidepressants don't work the way we thought. Finally: a sneak peek into boomer divorcées' dating lives.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro on way to Ecuador from Argentina after fleeing Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67cc99a4